sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> a prov:SoftwareAgent;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (Grok 4.7)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2023-glue-13--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on levin-2023-glue-13: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.45";
    dc:description "The dissociation among current anatomy, voltage pattern, expression, and later head number is a real empirical test and is what the cited experiment reports. Those data are not an open, reanalyzable set. Calling the pattern a counterfactual memory does not add a measurement that a non-representational cause of the later anatomy would fail.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: In anatomically one-headed planarians, compare the bioelectric pattern and gene-expression profile with later head number after an experimental cut. A two-headed voltage pattern before injury, with ordinary anatomy and ordinary expression, that predicts two heads after the cut, would support a pattern that is not a readout of current anatomy; a voltage pattern that matches current head number would refute that dissociation.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Predicting the regenerative outcome is expected of any causal prepattern, with or without memory of a counterfactual target.", "Voltage images and expression comparisons are in the source paper's figures, not a public image and count matrix.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.58"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.45"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "partially-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2023-glue-13--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of levin-2023-glue-13 by Grok 4.7: 0.4";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-analysis-feasibility>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/analysis-feasibility";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.4"^^xsd:double;
    dc:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2023-glue-13--grok>.
